#: admin/views/settings.php:36
msgid "Automatically detects search engine crawlers (Googlebot, Bingbot, etc.) and skips the banner for them. Improves SEO by serving cleaner HTML to crawlers. Note: with Cache Compatibility Mode enabled the bot-skip is bypassed — cached pages must stay identical for every visitor, so bots receive the banner too."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:42
msgid "Push consent events to GTM Data Layer"
msgstr "Verstuur toestemminggebeurtenissen naar GTM Data Layer"

#: admin/views/settings.php:44
msgid "Pushes a faz_consent_update event with per-category granted/denied values to window.dataLayer after each consent action. Enable if you use Google Tag Manager."
msgstr "Pusht een faz_consent_update event met per-categorie toegestane/geweigerde waarden naar window.dataLayer na elke toestemmingsactie. Activeer dit als je Google Tag Manager gebruikt."

#: admin/views/settings.php:50
msgid "Ad-blocker compatibility mode"
msgstr "Ad-blocker compatibiliteitsmodus"

#: admin/views/settings.php:52
msgid "Serves every frontend bundle (banner, accessibility, GCM, TCF, WP Consent API and Microsoft consent) through generic inline handles so plugin-URL filter rules cannot block only part of the consent runtime."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:58
msgid "Keep banner visible against ad blockers"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:60
msgid "If an ad blocker's cosmetic filter list hides the consent banner (some lists hide any element whose name contains \"cookie\" or \"consent\"), this re-asserts the banner's visibility once, shortly after it loads, so the legally required notice is not suppressed. It never forces interaction and respects a visitor who has already accepted, rejected or dismissed. This is different from Ad-blocker compatibility mode above, which stops the banner script itself from being blocked."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:66
msgid "Enable per-service consent"
msgstr "Per-dienst toestemming activeren"

#: admin/views/settings.php:68
msgid "When enabled, visitors can accept or reject individual services (e.g., Google Analytics, YouTube) instead of entire categories. Services detected by the scanner are shown immediately, and embedded providers blocked at runtime are revealed when the browser sees them on the page. This keeps the preference center present-aware but makes it more complex."
msgstr "Wanneer ingeschakeld, kunnen bezoekers individuele diensten accepteren of weigeren (bijv. Google Analytics, YouTube) in plaats van volledige categorieën. Diensten die door de scanner zijn gedetecteerd worden meteen getoond, en ingesloten providers die tijdens runtime worden geblokkeerd verschijnen zodra de browser ze op de pagina ziet. Zo blijft het voorkeurscentrum bewust van wat echt aanwezig is, maar wordt het complexer."

#: admin/views/settings.php:96
msgid "Enable per-cookie consent"
msgstr "Toestemming per cookie inschakelen"

#: admin/views/settings.php:98
msgid "Requires per-service consent. Adds a nested row for each cookie a service declares. First-party cookies that the site can write are enforced by client cleanup and the server-side shredder. Cookies set by embedded third-party services on their own domains (for example YouTube, Vimeo, Maps, social embeds) cannot be deleted individually by this site; those rows are shown as disabled and are controlled by allowing or blocking the whole embed."
msgstr "Vereist toestemming per service. Voegt een geneste rij toe voor elke cookie die een service declareert. First-party cookies die de site kan schrijven worden gehandhaafd via clientopruiming en de server-side shredder. Cookies die ingesloten diensten van derden op hun eigen domeinen plaatsen (bijvoorbeeld YouTube, Vimeo, Maps, sociale embeds) kunnen door deze site niet afzonderlijk worden verwijderd; die rijen worden uitgeschakeld getoond en worden beheerd door de volledige embed toe te staan of te blokkeren."

#: admin/views/settings.php:104
msgid "Share consent across subdomains"
msgstr "Toestemming delen via subdomeinen"

#: admin/views/settings.php:106
msgid "Scope the consent cookie to your registrable domain (e.g. .example.com) so it is shared across www, shop, app, etc. Recommended only when all subdomains belong to you and are covered by the same privacy policy. Public-suffix-aware for multi-level TLDs (.co.uk, .com.au)."
msgstr "Beperk de toestemmingscookie tot uw registreerbaar domein (bijv. .example.com) zodat deze gedeeld wordt via www, shop, app, enz. Alleen aanbevolen wanneer alle subdomeinen van u zijn en gedekt worden door hetzelfde privacybeleid. Ondersteunt public-suffix voor multi-level TLD’s (.co.uk, .com.au)."

#: admin/views/settings.php:112
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cache compatibility mode"
msgstr "Cache-compatibiliteitsmodus"

#: admin/views/settings.php:114
msgid "Keep a visitor-invariant page fully cacheable when jurisdiction enforcement is off and one banner law applies to everyone. When per-country enforcement is on, use the Cache-safe jurisdiction bootstrap under Jurisdiction &amp; Geo-routing instead. Developers can override the runtime with the <code>faz_geo_ruleset_runtime</code> filter. When this compatibility mode is active, it also pauses server-side A/B splitting and bot-specific output."
msgstr "Houdt een voor alle bezoekers identieke pagina volledig cachebaar wanneer handhaving per rechtsgebied uitstaat en één bannerwet voor iedereen geldt. Gebruik bij handhaving per land in plaats daarvan de cacheveilige bootstrap onder Rechtsgebied en geo-routering. Ontwikkelaars kunnen de runtime overschrijven met het filter <code>faz_geo_ruleset_runtime</code>. Wanneer deze compatibiliteitsmodus actief is, pauzeert hij ook server-side A/B-verdeling en botspecifieke uitvoer."

#: admin/views/settings.php:120
msgid "A/B test banner variants"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:122
msgid "Run two or more of your existing banners at the same time. A visitor is randomly shown one eligible variant without creating an experiment cookie before consent; after a choice, the banner slug in the consent record keeps the assignment stable. Acceptance rate per variant is reported on the Dashboard. Variants must use the same privacy-law and Do-Not-Sell model; country targeting is always respected, so the experiment can vary presentation but never a visitor's legal regime. <strong>Requires Cache Compatibility Mode above to be OFF</strong>, because a per-visitor split cannot run behind full-page caching."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:125
